swehouse.c: Porphyry cusps 11 and 12 grew from the Ascendant

They are offsets from the MC, so they grow from mc_speed.

    swetest -b1.1.2000 -ut12:00 -house13.4,52.5,O -speed
      house 11  687 38 11.2999  ->  426 54 36.0233
      house 12  774 32 43.0587  ->  513 49  7.7822

Five house systems fall back to Porphyry inside the polar circle and inherit
these speeds, so the same defect shows through any of them there.

Part of an eight-step series. Applied in order, the eight produce a file
byte-identical to the single patch "swehouse.c: compute house cusp speeds
analytically"; take either the series or that patch, not both. Every step
compiles. Steps 01 to 06 also apply to a clean tree on their own, so any one of
them can be taken without the rest; 07 needs 01 to 05, not 06; 08 needs all seven to link. Do not
drop 02 or 04 from the middle: nothing else needs them, so the result still
builds clean and is quietly wrong.

---
 swehouse.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
diff --git a/swehouse.c b/swehouse.c
index 5f750e4..668752a 100644
--- a/swehouse.c
+++ b/swehouse.c
@@ -1470,6 +1470,11 @@ porphyry:
     hsp->cusp[3] = swe_degnorm(hsp->ac + (180 - acmc) / 3 * 2);
     hsp->cusp[11] = swe_degnorm(hsp->mc + acmc / 3);
     hsp->cusp[12] = swe_degnorm(hsp->mc + acmc / 3 * 2);
+    /* Porphyry trisects each ecliptic quadrant equally, so every cusp is the
+     * Ascendant or the MC plus a fixed fraction of the quadrant acmc and the
+     * speeds follow directly. Cusps 11 and 12 are offsets from the MC and
+     * grow from mc_speed; before this patch they grew from ac_speed, which
+     * was wrong. */
     if (hsp->do_hspeed) {
       double q1_speed = hsp->ac_speed - hsp->mc_speed;	// rate of growth of quadrant 1
       // double q4_speed = hsp->mc_speed - hsp->ac_speed;	// rate of growth of quadrant 4
@@ -1477,8 +1482,10 @@ porphyry:
       hsp->cusp_speed[10] = hsp->mc_speed; // dito
       hsp->cusp_speed[2] = hsp->ac_speed  - q1_speed / 3;
       hsp->cusp_speed[3] = hsp->ac_speed  - q1_speed / 3 * 2;
-      hsp->cusp_speed[11] = hsp->ac_speed  + q1_speed / 3;
-      hsp->cusp_speed[12] = hsp->ac_speed  + q1_speed / 3 * 2;
+      /* cusps 11 and 12 are offsets from the MC, not from the Ascendant,
+       * so they grow from mc_speed. q1_speed is d(acmc)/dt. */
+      hsp->cusp_speed[11] = hsp->mc_speed  + q1_speed / 3;
+      hsp->cusp_speed[12] = hsp->mc_speed  + q1_speed / 3 * 2;
     }
     break;
   case 'Q':	/* Pullen sinusoidal ratio */
